.TH REMOTECONNECT 1 "May 2026" "dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
remoteConnect \- interactive SSH bootstrap and managed host alias workflow
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B remoteConnect
.RI [ new | list | edit | delete | log | show ]
.br
.B remoteConnect
help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B remoteConnect
creates and maintains SSH host entries in
.I ~/.ssh/config,
installs public keys for passwordless login, and optionally creates shell aliases in
.I ~/.zshrc.local.
.PP
It supports interactive setup for new hosts and management commands for listing, editing, deleting, and viewing logs for remoteConnect-managed entries.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B new
Runs interactive setup for a new managed host alias.
Prompts for server label, SSH alias, local host (optional), secondary remote/VPN host (optional), remote user, port, optional gateway alias, and key path.
.TP
.B list
Lists remoteConnect-managed aliases.
Use
.B list --commands
for resolved command details, route data, and shell alias status.
.TP
.B edit
Edits an existing managed alias in place.
Supports:
.B remoteConnect edit
or
.B remoteConnect edit ALIAS.
.TP
.B delete
Deletes a managed alias and its matching remoteConnect-created shell alias.
.TP
.B log
Shows log entries.
Examples:
.B remoteConnect log
,
.B remoteConnect log -t 100
,
.B remoteConnect log 100
.TP
.B show
Alias for
.B log.
.TP
.B help
Shows usage help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/config
Managed host entries are appended with marker lines:
.br
# Server: SERVER_NAME
.TP
.I ~/.zshrc.local
Optional shell alias blocks are appended:
.br
# Created by remoteConnect
.br
alias ALIAS_NAME="ssh HOST_ALIAS"
.TP
.I ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/remoteConnect/remoteConnect.log
Persistent operational log.
.TP
.I dotfiles/bin/ssh-select-host
Helper used for dynamic host preference and reachability checks.
.SH ROUTING
Supports local-only, secondary-only, and local+secondary (dynamic preference) host selection.
.PP
When a gateway alias is provided, managed SSH entries include
.B ProxyJump
and bootstrap key installation uses the same route.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Operation failed (validation, network, auth, or update error).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown command or missing required argument).
.SH EXAMPLES
.B remoteConnect new
.br
.B remoteConnect list --commands
.br
.B remoteConnect edit proxmox
.br
.B remoteConnect delete
.br
.B remoteConnect log -t 75
.SH SECURITY
Sets secure SSH directory and config permissions, validates alias names, avoids overwriting existing aliases on create, and cleans up keys generated during failed setup.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh-config (5),
.BR ssh-copy-id (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1)
